            <ArticleTitle>[Easyhalers in practice for treating patients with asthma].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>98-101</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A comparative investigation was conducted to study the therapeutic effect of using two powder inhalers (the new-generation device--an easyhaler as well as an aerolyser inhaler) in daily practice for treating patients with moderate asthma. It showed the pharmacological equivalence, efficiency, and safety of applying a combination of the easyhalers budesonide and formoterol, as well as the simplicity and convenience to use the inhalers of this type.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
